//! check: run(exit=1, stdout="handled: again\nerror: exists")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: std.fs, err.row, err.propagate, err.else
//!
//! The `exists` litmus — one of the two tags s90 added to this module's
//! vocabulary — in both directions a caller can take it: an `else` that
//! turns the miss into a value and lets the program continue, and a `?`
//! that propagates it out of `main`, where the process outcome NAMES the
//! tag on stdout and exits 1.
//!
//! That last line is how this rig witnesses a tag's IDENTITY, and it is
//! the only way that is worth anything: a handler asserting its own
//! reading of which tag fired is this repository talking to itself,
//! while `error: exists` is the toolchain naming it (§14's sc14 rule,
//! learned from F-0079). It matters more here than usual, because
//! `exists` is a row tag whose name is also a `pub fn` in the module
//! that raises it — `fs.exists` — and F-0036 says a colliding tag can
//! resolve to the function and ride out as a VALUE with no `else`
//! firing. This file is the standing measurement that it does not: the
//! `else` fires, and the record says `exists` rather than exiting 0 with
//! a function in its hand.
//!
//! Deterministic on any host: the directory is created by the line
//! before, inside a scratch directory staging has just cleared, so the
//! second creation cannot fail for any other reason. The program opens by
//! REMOVING that directory, because it ends by riding its tag out and so
//! never reaches a cleanup line, while the rig stages once and runs three
//! lanes in the one directory — without the clear, the second lane meets a
//! world the first one left behind. (That note is in this header because
//! `wolf fmt` splits a dotted call under a `//` comment, F-0016, and fmt
//! is law, D34.)
//!
//! `create_dir_all` deliberately has NO `exists` row and is not tested
//! here for one: it is idempotent by contract, and
//! `directories_and_metadata.lu` calls it twice on one path and expects
//! success.

use std.fs

fn main() -> !int {
    let d = "already-here"
    fs.remove_dir(d) else |_| {}
    fs.create_dir(d)?
    var again = "not-handled"
    fs.create_dir(d) else |_| {
        again = "again"
    }
    print("handled: {again}")
    fs.create_dir(d)?
    print("unreachable")
    0
}
